"Lie back, lie back! You just keeled over. Gradually, too. That's serious. Do you want a drink of water, or a doctor, or brandy?"[^doctor]
"I'm good."
[@ I'm not thinking this is all that making Martinius's alignment good accomplished, although it could be. I just thought it would be funny.]

[^doctor]: A drink of doctor away keeps the apple away.[$ This means that if you consume a doctor's blood, you can purge yourself of original sin.[$ Although, as is kind of pertinent for this little section, there are easier ways to become good. For some people.][$ Also this perpetuates the common misconception that the fruit of the Tree of the Knowledge of Good and Evil was an apple. But I've committed graver sins to justify funnier jokes. ~C]]
